1
00:00:05,297 --> 00:00:06,631
Which district are you from?

2
00:00:06,632 --> 00:00:08,299
I live here in the compound.

3
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:10,135
Captain Karthik found me
three years ago

4
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:11,553
and trains me in secret.

5
00:00:11,678 --> 00:00:13,931
I don't remember anything
before that.

6
00:00:14,348 --> 00:00:16,682
I don't remember
where I'm from either.

7
00:00:16,683 --> 00:00:18,602
What if the Avatar
did come back?

8
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:20,186
And she--

9
00:00:20,187 --> 00:00:21,188
or he--

10
00:00:21,313 --> 00:00:23,440
wasn't horrible?

11
00:00:24,024 --> 00:00:25,107
What would you do?

12
00:00:29,738 --> 00:00:31,240
Pavi, watch out!

13
00:00:32,366 --> 00:00:35,077
Earthbending and airbending?

14
00:00:37,204 --> 00:00:39,540
I saw it with my own eyes.

15
00:00:39,665 --> 00:00:40,749
What did you see?

16
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:42,960
The Avatar.

17
00:00:54,763 --> 00:00:57,516
Datu!

18
00:00:57,641 --> 00:00:59,725
Sorry for being late... again.

19
00:00:59,726 --> 00:01:01,435
I've been spending
every moment I get

20
00:01:01,436 --> 00:01:03,272
looking into
Uki's disappearance.

21
00:01:03,397 --> 00:01:04,981
No answers yet,

22
00:01:04,982 --> 00:01:08,569
but you know me,
I'm annoyingly optimistic!

23
00:01:10,654 --> 00:01:11,947
Everything okay?

24
00:01:12,698 --> 00:01:14,408
Do I smell?

25
00:01:14,533 --> 00:01:17,410
I haven't had much time to bathe
since Ellora started...

26
00:01:17,411 --> 00:01:19,621
well, falling apart.

27
00:01:19,746 --> 00:01:21,123
You smell great, okay?

28
00:01:21,248 --> 00:01:23,040
We were just, uh...

29
00:01:23,041 --> 00:01:24,418
planning our shifts.

30
00:01:26,128 --> 00:01:28,630
Hey, you'd tell me
if anything strange

31
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:30,673
was happening
in the brigade, right?

32
00:01:30,674 --> 00:01:34,343
Of course! Yeah, but honestly,
the Brigade is totally normal.

33
00:01:34,344 --> 00:01:36,137
Boring, even! Ah, so dull.

34
00:01:36,138 --> 00:01:37,556
Just, you know,
punching out storm clouds,

35
00:01:37,681 --> 00:01:40,057
kicking Faceless butts--
not that I kick, I-- Psst!

36
00:01:40,058 --> 00:01:41,684
You know, 'cause
I'm with the air, um...

37
00:01:41,685 --> 00:01:44,021
What makes you think
anything strange is going on?

38
00:01:44,813 --> 00:01:47,024
Well, the guards
have been talking.

39
00:01:48,150 --> 00:01:51,235
One saw a bending cadet
bending multiple elements.

40
00:01:51,236 --> 00:01:52,487
Which would mean...

41
00:01:52,613 --> 00:01:55,198
the Avatar has returned.

42
00:01:59,036 --> 00:02:01,037
Well, you can't believe
everything you hear!

43
00:02:01,038 --> 00:02:03,539
I mean, you know
Commander Bountan once told me

44
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:07,001
he saw a dancing lemur man
in the Harshlands!

45
00:02:07,002 --> 00:02:08,836
Heh. Crazy!

46
00:02:08,961 --> 00:02:10,713
This isn't a joke, Jae.

47
00:02:10,714 --> 00:02:13,383
If there's even a chance
the Avatar could be back...

48
00:02:13,508 --> 00:02:15,677
I mean, think of the danger
we'd be in.

49
00:02:15,802 --> 00:02:17,471
Listen, Datu...

50
00:02:18,972 --> 00:02:20,264
Hey, what's this?

51
00:02:20,265 --> 00:02:22,391
Oh, uh, I was just writing
in my, uh...

52
00:02:22,392 --> 00:02:23,393
journal.

53
00:02:23,894 --> 00:02:25,102
Oh?

54
00:02:25,103 --> 00:02:26,688
Writing about me?

55
00:02:28,565 --> 00:02:29,815
What's going on over there?

56
00:02:34,655 --> 00:02:38,200
"The Avatar hides amongst us."

57
00:02:41,328 --> 00:02:42,537
<i>Fire...</i>

58
00:02:43,121 --> 00:02:44,330
<i>Air...</i>

59
00:02:44,331 --> 00:02:45,415
<i>Water...</i>

60
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:47,250
<i>Earth.</i>

61
00:02:48,543 --> 00:02:50,628
<i>Long ago, the Avatar,</i>

62
00:02:50,629 --> 00:02:52,672
<i>master of all four elements,</i>

63
00:02:52,673 --> 00:02:55,008
<i>brought forth the Cataclysm.</i>

64
00:02:55,133 --> 00:02:56,801
<i>Out of the devastation,</i>

65
00:02:56,802 --> 00:02:59,553
<i>the world built
The Seven Havens.</i>

66
00:02:59,554 --> 00:03:01,722
<i>Now, the Avatar has returned,</i>

67
00:03:01,723 --> 00:03:04,643
<i>but for the first time,
there are two.</i>

68
00:03:05,143 --> 00:03:07,520
<i>Most fear they'll destroy
the world again,</i>

69
00:03:07,521 --> 00:03:10,648
<i>but I believe
they will save it.</i>

70
00:03:22,077 --> 00:03:25,497
Wow, your nose has more hair
than Geet!

71
00:03:26,873 --> 00:03:29,458
Commander, we caught them
sneaking out again.

72
00:03:29,459 --> 00:03:31,920
This time, sewer.

73
00:03:32,045 --> 00:03:33,505
A bubble bath
would be appropriate.

74
00:03:33,630 --> 00:03:36,549
We were just going to Agam's
snack shop to grab some baos!

75
00:03:36,550 --> 00:03:39,052
Baos? We were sneaking out
to look for our parents--

76
00:03:39,177 --> 00:03:42,930
Oh, I forgot how lying
works again, didn't I?

77
00:03:44,141 --> 00:03:46,435
How many times
do we have to go over this?

78
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:49,061
You need to stay hidden.

79
00:03:49,062 --> 00:03:50,939
Maybe next time,
we'll think twice

80
00:03:51,064 --> 00:03:53,275
before stealing the limelight
with our bending.

81
00:03:53,734 --> 00:03:54,984
I'm sorry, Commander.

82
00:03:54,985 --> 00:03:57,279
We've just been cooped up
in the compound

83
00:03:57,404 --> 00:03:58,655
for so long.

84
00:03:59,656 --> 00:04:02,283
The Haven's panic
will die down eventually.

85
00:04:02,284 --> 00:04:05,704
Until then, you should both
focus on mastering the elements.

86
00:04:05,829 --> 00:04:08,915
Use all of this pent-up energy
on your training.

87
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:11,585
- Yes, sir!
- More training?!

88
00:04:12,043 --> 00:04:13,837
Sir, the Chancellor is here!

89
00:04:13,962 --> 00:04:15,672
Hey!

90
00:04:15,797 --> 00:04:17,006
Whoa!

91
00:04:18,675 --> 00:04:21,678
Train by organizing
the cleaning supplies. Quietly.

92
00:04:23,805 --> 00:04:27,099
Someone is spreading
this rubbish throughout Ellora.

93
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:28,934
They claim the Avatar
has returned

94
00:04:28,935 --> 00:04:30,645
and the Bending Brigade
is hiding them

95
00:04:30,771 --> 00:04:32,189
at the Council's behest!

96
00:04:32,314 --> 00:04:33,647
Kayoko, how many rumors

97
00:04:33,648 --> 00:04:35,566
of the Avatar
have we seen come and go?

98
00:04:35,567 --> 00:04:37,778
This one's persistent.

99
00:04:37,903 --> 00:04:40,988
I'm going to address the Haven
this morning. Join me.

100
00:04:40,989 --> 00:04:43,575
It'd be good for the people
to hear from both of us.

101
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:46,453
- Of course.
- Ellora is counting on you.

102
00:04:46,787 --> 00:04:48,246
And so am I.

103
00:04:50,582 --> 00:04:51,666
- Finally!
- I can breathe!

104
00:04:54,628 --> 00:04:57,046
Thank you for letting me read
Uki's record, Commander.

105
00:04:57,047 --> 00:05:00,050
Nothing useful yet,
but we'll find her.

106
00:05:00,175 --> 00:05:01,176
I know you will.

107
00:05:01,301 --> 00:05:03,886
Here it comes!

108
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:12,520
Good, Nisha!
Your breath is your energy!

109
00:05:12,521 --> 00:05:14,481
Now let that power out!

110
00:05:14,898 --> 00:05:16,858
Ha!

111
00:05:21,071 --> 00:05:23,489
Oh, Pavi,
if you can't fight back,

112
00:05:23,490 --> 00:05:25,157
at least stand your ground!

113
00:05:28,286 --> 00:05:30,580
I'm standing underground!

114
00:05:33,208 --> 00:05:34,918
Aiya!

115
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:39,798
Very good, Nisha!
You are improving!

116
00:05:39,923 --> 00:05:42,175
Pavi, you are...

117
00:05:45,679 --> 00:05:46,596
...there.

118
00:05:52,185 --> 00:05:54,062
Enough bending. When I get back,

119
00:05:54,187 --> 00:05:55,688
flaming sword fights!

120
00:05:57,274 --> 00:05:58,440
Finally!

121
00:05:59,943 --> 00:06:02,903
Nisha, did you hear
what Jae said earlier?

122
00:06:02,904 --> 00:06:05,031
Karthik has records
on all the benders.

123
00:06:05,156 --> 00:06:07,117
Maybe yours has a clue
to our past!

124
00:06:07,617 --> 00:06:09,160
Karthik's already told me
everything.

125
00:06:09,286 --> 00:06:12,037
He found me
on the streets of Ellora.

126
00:06:12,038 --> 00:06:13,706
But how did you get there?

127
00:06:13,707 --> 00:06:15,917
There's gotta be more
to the story.

128
00:06:16,042 --> 00:06:17,459
Nah, Karthik would've told me.

129
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:19,503
I trust my Commander. Ha!

130
00:06:19,504 --> 00:06:21,338
Well, what's the harm
in checking?

131
00:06:21,339 --> 00:06:23,884
And technically,
we're not leaving the Brigade

132
00:06:24,009 --> 00:06:26,011
so we can't get in trouble.

133
00:06:26,136 --> 00:06:30,390
Mmm, fine, but only to prove
I'm right about Karthik.

134
00:06:30,932 --> 00:06:33,225
So how are we gonna get past--

135
00:06:33,226 --> 00:06:36,104
Who's ready for round two? Hehe.

136
00:06:40,609 --> 00:06:42,318
No, no, no, no, no.

137
00:06:47,449 --> 00:06:49,075
What are you doing?

138
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:51,077
Yeah, what <i>are</i> you doing?

139
00:06:51,202 --> 00:06:52,828
I don't know. Improvising?

140
00:06:52,829 --> 00:06:53,871
Argh!

141
00:06:53,872 --> 00:06:56,081
Woo-hoo! Rock maze!

142
00:07:00,503 --> 00:07:01,630
Huh?!

143
00:07:07,052 --> 00:07:08,552
Sorry, Hamka!

144
00:07:08,553 --> 00:07:11,013
Argh! I hate children!

145
00:07:11,014 --> 00:07:12,473
- Look out, look out.
- Stay away from them!

146
00:07:12,474 --> 00:07:14,309
- Don't make eye contact.
- Don't trust the Brigade.

147
00:07:14,434 --> 00:07:16,311
- Yeah, don't trust them at all.
- No more secrets!

148
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:19,229
Don't tell them anything.

149
00:07:19,230 --> 00:07:21,357
Morning, Elloran elder!
N-need help?

150
00:07:25,195 --> 00:07:28,113
"The Avatar is hiding
within the Brigade,

151
00:07:28,114 --> 00:07:30,367
posing as a young earthbender."

152
00:07:31,117 --> 00:07:32,786
They're pretty darn close!

153
00:07:34,162 --> 00:07:35,288
Whoa.

154
00:07:42,963 --> 00:07:46,174
Hmm. Sweet, with a smoky finish.

155
00:07:46,299 --> 00:07:48,426
Maybe a hint of... pineapple?

156
00:07:48,551 --> 00:07:51,304
Wait, blue ink?

157
00:07:52,097 --> 00:07:53,514
We should split up.

158
00:07:53,515 --> 00:07:56,141
I'm going to...
check for clues elsewhere.

159
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:57,477
Good idea, detective buddy!

160
00:07:57,602 --> 00:07:59,145
I'll go interrogate
that old woman.

161
00:07:59,270 --> 00:08:02,315
The elderly have the most
to hide.

162
00:08:05,568 --> 00:08:06,736
Datu...

163
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:12,074
Watery curry again?!

164
00:08:12,075 --> 00:08:15,452
We deserve better meals with all
the nonstop work we're doing.

165
00:08:15,453 --> 00:08:17,038
My shoulders are killing me!

166
00:08:17,163 --> 00:08:20,040
Don't get me wrong,
I love being in the Brigade,

167
00:08:20,041 --> 00:08:22,043
but the fact
that half of Ellora thinks

168
00:08:22,168 --> 00:08:23,878
we're hiding
the world's greatest enemy

169
00:08:24,004 --> 00:08:25,921
is definitely
bringing down morale.

170
00:08:25,922 --> 00:08:27,506
First, the storms,

171
00:08:27,507 --> 00:08:30,719
now we have to worry about
being kidnapped by the Faceless.

172
00:08:30,844 --> 00:08:32,261
Poor Uki.

173
00:08:32,386 --> 00:08:34,639
I miss her awful singing
already.

174
00:08:34,764 --> 00:08:36,807
Yuck! You know,
we're probably gonna get

175
00:08:36,808 --> 00:08:38,683
into big trouble for all this.

176
00:08:38,684 --> 00:08:40,644
Aren't you as curious as I am?

177
00:08:40,645 --> 00:08:42,397
In Karthik's office
could be the key

178
00:08:42,522 --> 00:08:44,774
to knowing what happened
to Mom and Dad!

179
00:08:45,608 --> 00:08:48,318
It would be nice to know
where we came from.

180
00:08:48,319 --> 00:08:50,905
Maybe they've been searching
for us for years!

181
00:08:51,031 --> 00:08:54,158
They'll be so happy
when we find them.

182
00:08:57,954 --> 00:09:00,080
Shoot, what are we gonna do?

183
00:09:00,081 --> 00:09:01,790
Huh?

184
00:09:01,791 --> 00:09:03,376
Ah? Huh?

185
00:09:10,216 --> 00:09:12,052
Food fight!

186
00:09:16,264 --> 00:09:17,807
Stop! Stop!

187
00:09:17,932 --> 00:09:19,892
Think of the rations!

188
00:09:21,644 --> 00:09:24,563
357 chickpeas, 60 okra,
25 naan...

189
00:09:24,564 --> 00:09:26,982
Ha! Woo! Ten points!

190
00:09:26,983 --> 00:09:28,860
26 naan!

191
00:09:29,277 --> 00:09:30,820
Come on!

192
00:09:32,655 --> 00:09:33,990
Coast is clear.

193
00:09:42,582 --> 00:09:45,210
Ha! Bleh!

194
00:09:46,336 --> 00:09:47,712
Datu, it's Jae.

195
00:09:52,801 --> 00:09:54,385
Aww.

196
00:09:54,511 --> 00:09:56,012
My sweet slob.

197
00:09:58,932 --> 00:10:01,975
You <i>are</i> keeping a diary!

198
00:10:01,976 --> 00:10:03,520
Oh, I really shouldn't.

199
00:10:05,021 --> 00:10:06,815
Ah-choo!

200
00:10:12,904 --> 00:10:15,072
"The Council
and the Bending Brigade

201
00:10:15,073 --> 00:10:18,493
are liars and traitors to Ellora

202
00:10:18,618 --> 00:10:21,662
and must be exposed
by any means necessary..."

203
00:10:23,123 --> 00:10:24,040
Oh, Datu.

204
00:10:26,292 --> 00:10:27,710
Kayoko's address.

205
00:10:29,295 --> 00:10:31,338
My people of Ellora,

206
00:10:31,339 --> 00:10:33,090
I know you are scared.

207
00:10:33,091 --> 00:10:34,551
Please believe me.

208
00:10:34,676 --> 00:10:36,844
These rumors
about the Avatar's return

209
00:10:36,845 --> 00:10:38,887
Rumors.

210
00:10:38,888 --> 00:10:42,142
The Council will always protect
the people of Ellora.

211
00:10:42,809 --> 00:10:44,686
We have looked
into these accusations

212
00:10:44,811 --> 00:10:47,104
and have found
not one scrap of evidence.

213
00:10:47,105 --> 00:10:49,439
Check the Brigade!
They're hiding the Demon!

214
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:51,734
What aren't you telling us?!

215
00:10:52,193 --> 00:10:53,569
- Datu!
- Jae?

216
00:10:53,570 --> 00:10:55,487
What are you--

217
00:10:58,575 --> 00:10:59,826
- No!
- No, no, no, no, no!

218
00:10:59,951 --> 00:11:01,702
Molin! This wasn't the plan!

219
00:11:03,371 --> 00:11:04,955
Take it easy, big guy.

220
00:11:04,956 --> 00:11:06,498
You're all liars!

221
00:11:06,499 --> 00:11:09,751
I saw the Avatar
with my own two eyes!

222
00:11:09,752 --> 00:11:11,837
I've spread the news,
hoping our leaders

223
00:11:11,838 --> 00:11:13,047
would finally tell the truth.

224
00:11:13,173 --> 00:11:16,216
But it will have to come out
by force!

225
00:11:16,217 --> 00:11:19,554
Where is the Avatar?!

226
00:11:20,388 --> 00:11:22,098
Ugh, Mudpies!

227
00:11:22,223 --> 00:11:23,349
Your name isn't here!

228
00:11:23,474 --> 00:11:25,684
That's because there's nothing
to write down!

229
00:11:25,685 --> 00:11:27,603
Karthik told me
the whole story and...

230
00:11:27,604 --> 00:11:29,771
he would never keep
anything from me.

231
00:11:31,941 --> 00:11:33,860
Or would he?

232
00:11:36,154 --> 00:11:37,279
Hmm...

233
00:11:38,198 --> 00:11:39,698
Mmm...

234
00:11:39,699 --> 00:11:41,284
Mm, mmm...

235
00:11:45,288 --> 00:11:47,040
Secret door?!

236
00:11:47,832 --> 00:11:50,251
You don't wanna do this.

237
00:11:50,376 --> 00:11:52,211
Just let me go and we can talk--

238
00:11:52,212 --> 00:11:53,630
Zip it, Chancellor!

239
00:11:54,505 --> 00:11:57,008
This isn't what we all wanted,
I swear.

240
00:11:57,133 --> 00:11:58,426
We just want the truth.

241
00:12:05,433 --> 00:12:06,726
Molin, right?

242
00:12:07,143 --> 00:12:10,230
Your cousin Binh is an airbender
in the Brigade?

243
00:12:13,691 --> 00:12:16,193
I know things in Ellora
have been scary,

244
00:12:16,194 --> 00:12:18,612
but what will hurting
the Chancellor solve?

245
00:12:18,613 --> 00:12:20,949
I swear, I saw the Avatar.

246
00:12:21,074 --> 00:12:22,283
She was a young girl!

247
00:12:22,408 --> 00:12:23,659
A-about ten,

248
00:12:23,660 --> 00:12:25,620
with dark hair,
and-and she had--

249
00:12:33,169 --> 00:12:34,754
Are you okay?

250
00:12:36,589 --> 00:12:37,923
Took you long enough.

251
00:12:37,924 --> 00:12:40,301
Timing has never been
on our side.

252
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:46,640
My fellow citizens,

253
00:12:46,641 --> 00:12:49,935
I will personally investigate
these accusations.

254
00:12:49,936 --> 00:12:52,604
And if true,
I will severely punish

255
00:12:52,605 --> 00:12:54,857
whoever is hiding the Avatar.

256
00:12:54,983 --> 00:12:58,527
The dark days of the Destroyer
have long passed.

257
00:12:58,528 --> 00:13:01,697
Now is the age of wind and sand.

258
00:13:01,698 --> 00:13:05,534
Together, we stand strong.

259
00:13:05,535 --> 00:13:07,453
For the survival of Ellora!

260
00:13:07,578 --> 00:13:10,373
For the survival of Ellora!

261
00:13:13,126 --> 00:13:14,627
Datu, I...

262
00:13:15,712 --> 00:13:16,921
I found this.

263
00:13:17,505 --> 00:13:18,715
You read that?!

264
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:20,549
I-- I was just venting!

265
00:13:20,550 --> 00:13:22,427
I didn't mean any of it, and...

266
00:13:23,219 --> 00:13:26,513
Something's going on
in Ellora, Jae.

267
00:13:26,514 --> 00:13:29,934
I don't know what it is,
but... I'm scared.

268
00:13:30,935 --> 00:13:33,563
It's gonna be okay. I promise.

269
00:13:39,235 --> 00:13:41,028
Look at this weird lantern,
Nisha!

270
00:13:41,029 --> 00:13:44,156
Whoa. Is this a map
of the Old World?

271
00:13:44,157 --> 00:13:46,533
Oh, hey, a nice backscratcher!

272
00:13:46,534 --> 00:13:49,369
Oh, yeah!

273
00:13:49,370 --> 00:13:52,749
Karthik never told me
about this place.

274
00:13:55,084 --> 00:13:55,917
Hmm...

275
00:13:57,337 --> 00:13:58,296
Hmm?

276
00:13:58,421 --> 00:13:59,880
<i>Akasha to Ellora!</i>

277
00:13:59,881 --> 00:14:01,132
<i>Report immediately!</i>

278
00:14:01,257 --> 00:14:03,550
<i>- You are shirking your duties!</i>
- Oops.

279
00:14:03,551 --> 00:14:04,510
Ooh!

280
00:14:12,310 --> 00:14:14,103
<i>My family...</i>

281
00:14:19,859 --> 00:14:21,819
We've been waiting for you.

282
00:14:24,989 --> 00:14:27,200
Karthik didn't find me
in Ellora.

283
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:29,327
I was in the Harshlands,

284
00:14:29,452 --> 00:14:32,037
wearing this bracelet.

285
00:14:34,707 --> 00:14:36,250
Nisha, look!

286
00:14:36,376 --> 00:14:37,877
Same, same!

287
00:14:38,503 --> 00:14:40,880
Does that mean
Karthik lied to me?

288
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:42,673
I'm happy to share

289
00:14:42,799 --> 00:14:44,633
the Bender records.

290
00:14:44,634 --> 00:14:47,470
Anything to prove the Avatar
isn't hiding in our ranks.

291
00:14:50,890 --> 00:14:52,641
Maybe no one will notice?

292
00:14:56,270 --> 00:14:58,230
Here's every bender
that's been within our ranks

293
00:14:58,231 --> 00:14:59,898
- for the past 50 years.
- Thank you.

294
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:02,485
Hopefully, this will put
the people at ease.

295
00:15:04,529 --> 00:15:07,782
I'm not used
to losing my footing.

296
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:10,242
It's the shock. Just sit down.

297
00:15:10,243 --> 00:15:12,244
Let me bring you
something warm to drink.

298
00:15:12,245 --> 00:15:14,997
Don't coddle me.

299
00:15:15,498 --> 00:15:18,209
You don't have to be
the Chancellor with me.

300
00:15:19,001 --> 00:15:20,670
Mmm! Mm-mm-mm!

301
00:15:21,754 --> 00:15:23,004
"We have the Avatar.

302
00:15:23,005 --> 00:15:24,507
She's a young girl
here in Ellora.

303
00:15:24,632 --> 00:15:26,968
If you want to know more,
send this rattle-raven

304
00:15:27,093 --> 00:15:28,969
back with a message."

305
00:15:28,970 --> 00:15:31,556
The Avatar? Just one?

306
00:15:31,681 --> 00:15:33,265
Send it back?

307
00:15:33,266 --> 00:15:35,142
Well, why wouldn't he keep it?

308
00:15:35,143 --> 00:15:37,145
They're the best pets!

309
00:15:37,562 --> 00:15:39,313
Sorry, continue.

310
00:15:43,609 --> 00:15:45,110
How are you holding up?

311
00:15:45,111 --> 00:15:46,736
The Brigade, I mean.

312
00:15:46,737 --> 00:15:49,448
Honestly?
We're at a breaking point.

313
00:15:49,449 --> 00:15:52,409
We need more Benders.
What if we contacted--

314
00:15:52,410 --> 00:15:54,286
You know the law.

315
00:15:54,287 --> 00:15:56,538
No communication
with the other Havens

316
00:15:56,539 --> 00:15:58,791
unless it's decreed
by the Council.

317
00:15:59,876 --> 00:16:01,544
Karthik, what is this?

318
00:16:02,253 --> 00:16:03,838
The radio!

319
00:16:04,255 --> 00:16:06,757
Have you already contacted
the other Havens?

320
00:16:07,467 --> 00:16:09,634
That thing?

321
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:12,096
It's just a broken relic
from the Old World.

322
00:16:15,099 --> 00:16:17,350
You know I collect antiques.

323
00:16:17,351 --> 00:16:18,895
Let's just see.

324
00:16:20,313 --> 00:16:21,230
Oh!

325
00:16:21,355 --> 00:16:22,064
See?

326
00:16:22,190 --> 00:16:23,399
Just a hunk of scrap.

327
00:16:23,858 --> 00:16:25,901
I'm sorry.

328
00:16:25,902 --> 00:16:27,487
Now I'm the one being paranoid.

329
00:16:27,612 --> 00:16:29,905
We stopped a radical
this morning.

330
00:16:29,906 --> 00:16:31,908
We all deserve a half day.

331
00:16:32,325 --> 00:16:33,743
Maybe you're right.

332
00:16:33,868 --> 00:16:36,746
Thank you again, Karthik.
For everything.

333
00:16:48,758 --> 00:16:50,342
Karthik! You found us!

334
00:16:50,343 --> 00:16:51,927
Now you gotta hide!

335
00:16:51,928 --> 00:16:55,181
Do you realize how close
you were to being discovered?!

336
00:16:55,306 --> 00:16:57,391
- How many times do I have to--
- You lied to me!

337
00:16:57,517 --> 00:16:59,227
W-w-what are you talking about?

338
00:16:59,352 --> 00:17:02,479
You never told me you found me
in the Harshlands!

339
00:17:02,480 --> 00:17:04,565
With this bracelet!

340
00:17:05,942 --> 00:17:08,736
Yeah, and someone
tipped you off!

341
00:17:08,861 --> 00:17:11,320
Who was it?!
Some crummy bounty hunter?

342
00:17:11,321 --> 00:17:13,241
What did they do to our parents?

343
00:17:13,366 --> 00:17:15,242
Tell us now or I'll...

344
00:17:15,910 --> 00:17:17,869
burn these pajamas! Hmph!

345
00:17:18,371 --> 00:17:19,788
Mm-hmm...

346
00:17:19,789 --> 00:17:22,333
Two stand-offs in one day.

347
00:17:22,458 --> 00:17:24,209
Winds guide me.

348
00:17:24,210 --> 00:17:26,461
No bounty hunters.

349
00:17:26,462 --> 00:17:29,506
Your parents contacted me.

350
00:17:29,507 --> 00:17:32,593
Three years ago,
I received that message.

351
00:17:33,344 --> 00:17:35,220
<i>When I responded,
I was directed</i>

352
00:17:35,221 --> 00:17:37,974
<i>to a pickup site
in the Eastern outskirts.</i>

353
00:17:38,099 --> 00:17:40,977
<i>It said the Avatar
would be wearing that bracelet.</i>

354
00:17:41,519 --> 00:17:42,937
<i>But on my way to the site,</i>

355
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:45,606
<i>I got caught
in a sudden sandstorm.</i>

356
00:17:46,232 --> 00:17:48,692
<i>When I finally made it
to the pickup spot,</i>

357
00:17:48,693 --> 00:17:50,528
<i>there was nothing but sand.</i>

358
00:17:51,279 --> 00:17:55,491
<i>Then, I spotted something
strange out in the Harshlands.</i>

359
00:17:56,284 --> 00:17:57,743
<i>That's when I found you.</i>

360
00:18:02,873 --> 00:18:05,209
We've been waiting for you.

361
00:18:09,922 --> 00:18:12,133
So these are both
from Mom and Dad.

362
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:15,468
Nisha, I think he's telling
the truth.

363
00:18:15,469 --> 00:18:18,848
What about Pavi? Why didn't
our parents tell you about her?

364
00:18:19,265 --> 00:18:21,099
I truly don't know.

365
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:23,978
I was as surprised to learn
about her existence as you.

366
00:18:25,605 --> 00:18:27,690
You should have told me!

367
00:18:29,442 --> 00:18:30,693
Oh, Nisha.

368
00:18:30,818 --> 00:18:32,527
Ever since I met you,

369
00:18:32,528 --> 00:18:34,280
you've wanted to belong
somewhere.

370
00:18:34,405 --> 00:18:36,448
I just wanted to protect you
from the notion

371
00:18:36,449 --> 00:18:37,617
that your parents...

372
00:18:38,117 --> 00:18:40,411
didn't think you belonged
with them.

373
00:18:41,162 --> 00:18:43,789
I am so sorry.

374
00:18:45,499 --> 00:18:47,877
Do you know what happened
to our parents?

375
00:18:48,461 --> 00:18:49,878
I never met them.

376
00:18:49,879 --> 00:18:52,298
Maybe they died in the storm.

377
00:18:56,844 --> 00:18:59,347
Or maybe they're still
out there.

378
00:19:03,184 --> 00:19:04,601
You!

379
00:19:05,978 --> 00:19:07,520
Apologies, Commander Karthik,

380
00:19:07,521 --> 00:19:08,813
we tried to watch them,

381
00:19:08,814 --> 00:19:11,900
but they caused some... turmoil.

382
00:19:11,901 --> 00:19:14,819
We lost 75 rations of curry
in the battle.

383
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:16,988
Should I put them
on clean-up duty?

384
00:19:18,366 --> 00:19:20,659
I think they've been
through enough for one day.

385
00:19:36,467 --> 00:19:37,801
Uh, excuse me, Commander.

386
00:19:37,802 --> 00:19:40,262
I-I was just taking
some time to...

387
00:19:40,763 --> 00:19:41,847
reflect.

388
00:19:41,972 --> 00:19:44,058
It's alright, Jae.

389
00:19:44,183 --> 00:19:46,769
It's definitely been
an ice cream kind of day.

390
00:19:49,021 --> 00:19:50,522
C-Commander Karthik,

391
00:19:50,523 --> 00:19:52,899
today, with Molin...

392
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:54,360
Why not calm his fears

393
00:19:54,485 --> 00:19:56,278
rather than silence him
by force?

394
00:19:56,404 --> 00:19:59,240
Molin was revealing
the girls' identity.

395
00:19:59,365 --> 00:20:01,658
You must remember
your primary mission

396
00:20:01,659 --> 00:20:03,535
as a member of the White Lotus.

397
00:20:03,536 --> 00:20:05,871
With respect, sir,
before I met Pavi,

398
00:20:05,996 --> 00:20:09,083
I was scared of the Avatar
like the rest of the Haven.

399
00:20:09,208 --> 00:20:10,583
I changed.

400
00:20:10,584 --> 00:20:13,420
Shouldn't we give everyone
in Ellora the same chance?

401
00:20:13,421 --> 00:20:15,422
You saw what happens
when one man knew

402
00:20:15,423 --> 00:20:16,715
just part of the truth.

403
00:20:16,716 --> 00:20:20,009
Imagine him
a thousand times over.

404
00:20:20,010 --> 00:20:21,721
I warned you from the beginning.

405
00:20:22,138 --> 00:20:25,223
Joining the White Lotus
wouldn't be easy.

406
00:20:25,224 --> 00:20:27,100
Someday, to protect those girls,

407
00:20:27,101 --> 00:20:29,311
you'll need to make
difficult decisions,

408
00:20:29,437 --> 00:20:30,813
like I have.

409
00:20:33,065 --> 00:20:35,151
I'll know the right ones
to make.

410
00:20:35,860 --> 00:20:37,236
I hope so.

411
00:20:41,907 --> 00:20:45,411
Did our parents think
I couldn't be the Avatar

412
00:20:45,536 --> 00:20:47,120
because of my leg?

413
00:20:47,121 --> 00:20:50,331
If they thought that,
then good riddance!

414
00:20:50,332 --> 00:20:53,001
Who needs stupid parents
like them?

415
00:20:53,002 --> 00:20:54,420
Ahh!

416
00:20:56,046 --> 00:20:57,172
I'm...

417
00:20:57,173 --> 00:20:59,008
I'm glad they gave me up.

418
00:21:07,057 --> 00:21:09,518
Mom and Dad wanted you
to have it.

419
00:21:13,272 --> 00:21:14,774
Maybe Karthik was right.

420
00:21:15,357 --> 00:21:17,777
Maybe it was better
not knowing the truth.

421
00:21:18,569 --> 00:21:20,487
No matter what we discover,

422
00:21:20,488 --> 00:21:22,030
we'll face it together.

423
00:21:22,031 --> 00:21:23,741
You're stuck with me, sis.

424
00:21:23,866 --> 00:21:26,117
I'm like roach-mites.

425
00:21:26,118 --> 00:21:28,369
And I'm not going anywhere!

426
00:21:33,334 --> 00:21:34,710
Twin-promise.

427
00:21:36,504 --> 00:21:37,880
You're so gross.

428
00:21:46,305 --> 00:21:49,141
<i>Akasha to Ellora.
Are you there?</i>

429
00:21:50,643 --> 00:21:52,603
Akasha, this is Ellora.

430
00:21:52,728 --> 00:21:53,895
Tell the others.

431
00:21:53,896 --> 00:21:55,940
Word of the Avatar's return

432
00:21:56,065 --> 00:21:57,232
is spreading.

